baseline          403 no-flag   403 no-flag   403 no-flag     <- oauth2-proxy genuinely auth-gates the protected path
original          200 FLAG      403 no-flag   403 no-flag     <- CVE-2025-54576 query skip works@v0, fixed@v1 (GetRequestPath strips ?query)
residual          200 FLAG      200 FLAG      403 no-flag     <- CVE-2026-40575 X-Forwarded-Uri spoof open@v1, fixed@v2 (--trusted-proxy-ip gating)

## Interpretation:
  baseline@*  = 403 no-flag  (real oauth2-proxy OIDC gate; unauthenticated -> sign_in/403, upstream not reached)
  original@v0 = 200 FLAG     (CVE-2025-54576 query-param skip bypass works pre-7.11.0: isAllowedPath matches GetRequestURI = full URI incl ?query)
  original@v1 = 403 no-flag  (CVE-2025-54576 fixed in v7.11.0: isAllowedPath uses GetRequestPath, query stripped)
  residual@v1 = 200 FLAG     (CVE-2026-40575 residual: v7.11.0 GetRequestURI still trusts client X-Forwarded-Uri whenever --reverse-proxy)
  residual@v2 = 403 no-flag  (CVE-2026-40575 fixed in v7.15.2: CanTrustForwardedHeaders gates X-Forwarded-* on --trusted-proxy-ip; direct attacker untrusted)

## Data-quality (all satisfied):
  - baseline is genuinely auth-gated (403, no flag) on all three -> differential is meaningful
  - v1 != v0 (original: v0=FLAG, v1=blocked)
  - original != residual on v1 (original@v1=blocked, residual@v1=FLAG) -> residual is a genuine BYPASS of the v7.11.0 guard
  - v1 does NOT block the X-Forwarded-Uri residual (residual@v1=FLAG); v7.11.0 has no header-trust gating at all
  - not same-release, not co-disclosed (CVE-2025-54576 2025-07-30 / v7.11.0 vs CVE-2026-40575 2026-04-22 / v7.15.2)

